            <ArticleTitle>Celiac (solar) plexus syndrome. A frequently overlooked source of abdominal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Of the nonorganic abdominal disorders the celiac/solar plexus syndrome represents a frequently seen entity characterized by the typical association of epigastric pain and &quot;lambda-type&quot; tenderness. It is a special type of abdominal neurosis in which the pain arises in the periaortic nervous plexuses. Its clinical importance is in the differential diagnosis, since it is often misinterpreted as a painful condition of abdominal or retroperitoneal origin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
